  {
   "id": "T1dmBXKKAQAJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2019-05-09T22:26:54Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Rqtl2-disc] Re: how to fix the Error in scan1snps",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(83,101,121)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\">You inserted pseudomarkers </span></span></span><i style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"><br></i></p>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;font-family:Menlo;color:rgb(83,101,121)\"><i style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"><br></i></p><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(83,101,121)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><i style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"># Calculating genotype propabilities</i></span></p><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\r\n</span><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\">map &lt;- insert_pseudomarkers(cc$gmap, step=<span style=\"color:rgb(28,0,207)\">1</span>)</span></span></p><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\r\n</span><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(83,101,121)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><i style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"># use calc_genoprob() to calculate the QTL genotype probabilities.</i></span></p><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\r\n</span><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\">pr &lt;- calc_genoprob(cc, map, error_prob=<span style=\"color:rgb(28,0,207)\">0.002</span>)</span></span></p><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">\r\n</span><p style=\"margin:0px;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:12px;line-height:normal;color:rgb(83,101,121)\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><i style=\"background-color:rgb(243,243,243)\"># convert genotype<span>  </span>probabilities to allele probabilities</i></span></p></blockquote><br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div>so <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">pr</span> corresponds to <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">map</span> not <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">cc$pmap</span>. But to use <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">scan1snps()</span> you&#39;ll need the physical map.</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">    pmap &lt;- interp_map(map, cc$gmap, cc$pmap)</span></div><div><br></div><div>You should then be able to use <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">pmap</span> in the call to <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">scan1snps()</span>, where you were using <span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\">cc$pmap</span>.</div><div><br></div><div>karl<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
